I've had the same problem.  Quote du jour: `The best thing about Emacs
is the EDT emulation.'  Try <ESCAPE>-X-edt-emulation-on, which should
work in GNUEMACS after about version 19 or so.  I use it all the time when
I have to work under UNIX.  Of course, it's not as good as the original,
but it helps.  You might have some problems with the numeric keypad if
the keyboard is layed out differently than a VTxxx.  I you have the
patience, you can define the keys in the typical UNIX way, that is,
about 11 levels of software (hardware) higher than where this should be done
(see the relevant chapter in the UNIX HATERS' HANDBOOK) by playing
around with your xmodmap, .emacs and so on.

Hope this helps,

