dall@hfrd.dsto.gov.au wrote:
: We have a DECStation 5000/200 and we would like to use its monitor
: (19" Sony) on another machine.

: It appears that the scan rate on the monitor is lower than the new
: machine we wish to put it on. (We need 72Hz 1024 lines, whatever that
: works out to in horizontal scan rate). The monitor seems to "keep up"
: with the frequencies, but the horizonatl size is too small.  Is there
: some internal adjustment which can fix that?

Yes, there are a RAFT of internal adjustments.  You just have to take the
external plastic cover off, and there should be clearly marked holes in
the inner aluminum shield showing which adjustment is which.  If the
horizontal sweep rate is much faster than the monitor is rated for, it
may cause overheating of the sweep board, and possibly failure of the
monitor.


