In article <3b0564$kco@fozzy.aud.alcatel.com>, aldeav@aud.alcatel.com (Al V. Alder) writes:
>Could someone direct me to the documentation (perferrably electronic)
>that defines the key code that are generated for the above keyboards.
>If this information is in the FAQ for this group, then where do I get
>the FAQ?

Information like this should be in the FAQ.  There's always someone inventing
yet another terminal emulator for their PC, or trying to get their el-cheapo
shareware terminal emulator to emulate correctly, or whatever.

If you have access to a VAX/VMS system, type or print the file
SYS$SYSTEM:SMGTERMS.TXT.  This is a listing of all the escape and control
sequences that SMG knows how to send to a terminal, and what SMG can handle
from terminals.  While the format of this file doesn't exactly take one by the
hand (not that it's meant to), the format is fairly obvious to someone who
might be familiar with ANSI standard escape and control sequences, and just
needs to know the specifics.

