I have noticed that whenever I FTP large files, usually compressed
tar-files, between other Unix machines and OSF/1 V3.0, then the transfer
mode matters - if ASCII transfer mode is used, then some files
loses a few bytes, while the BINARY mode always makes identical copies.
This happens both when I GET files from Ultrix 4.2 and SunOS,
while between Ultrix and SunOS there is no such problem.

It was always my belief that the only difference between these modes,
with Unix at both ends of the link, was speed, that the ASCII transfer mode
has more overhead. However since there _is_ a difference - just what is
the difference? What about ASCII data from non-Unix machines?

I discovered this because Ultrix is not recognized as "UNIX" and the default
transfer mode is then ASCII...

