In article <3ar4dn$7ho@newsbf01.news.aol.com>, jonerich@aol.com (JonEricH)
writes:

|>Does anyone know of a product/protocol for the dynamic assignment of
|>DECNet phase IV addresses?


   I know of no product that does this for DECnet, though there is one
   package that does perform static DECnet address remapping.  (The
   DECnet address translation gateway.)  Since you are looking, you
   likely don't have a trivial network...

   Dynamic reassignment of DECnet addresses is likely to cause routing
   problems should any attempt be made to reassign addresses across
   DECnet areas -- areas must be contiguous, and nodes must be able
   to gain access to a same-area area router.

|>We're looking for BOOTP or DHCP-like functionality for mobile laptops that
|>need DECNet addresses.

   Consider using the RoamAbout Mobile and RoamAbout Transport products,
   and DEC TCP/IP (UCX) -- though these are IP, not DECnet, products.

|>It seems futile, given the relationship between ethernet addresses and
|>DECNet areas/nodes, but I thought I'd check.

   As previously mentioned, the linkage between the physical address
   and the DECnet address was removed in DECnet OSI -- DECnet OSI
   uses the hardware address. 

   DECnet is not tied to a hardware address.  The MOP subsystem does
   use the hardware address during down-line loading operations.


