One option is NTP, a pretty standard way to do distributed time
synchronization on TCP/IP based systems. Available over the Internet
for Unix systems pretty easily, and built into at least one TCP/IP
for VMS product (MultiNet). I think it's also in the Woolongong TCP/IP
product, though I doubt that it's in UCX. Running NTP gives you
automatic daylight savings time adjustment as well as time sychronization,
and it's a standard, widely available protocol, unlike whatever DTSS uses.

