You don't specify the address to boot from, the boot request goes out and
basically requests "can someone boot this poor machine?".  And if a kindly
system has the ethernet address of the MV2000 in its list of those it deigns
to speak to, lo the mv2000 will boot...	:-)

>We want to boot Ultrix, not VMS, if that matters...

Just use ris to install a distribution tape onto the 5000 system, then
add the mv2000 as a ris client and then boot the mv2000.

