In article <CzGxKv.KL3@cadre.com>, meh@cadre.com (Mike Hoover) writes:
> I have a question about the DEC RRD42 cdrom drive. Is
> this drive a single speed drive or double, triple?

  Single. It's a Sony CDU-541 with a 512-byte sector size instead of the more 
common 2048. Depending on your PC software, you might need to tell your CD-ROM
driver about the sector size *or* open the drive enclosure and cut the purple
wire loop on the connector that plugs into the drive's ID select plug. On a
real CDU-541 this would be parity enable/disable, while on a DEC RRD42 variant
it selects 512/2048 byte sector size.

