If you have never ported your application to another operating system (or
even other versions of UNIX) you may discover a lot of UNIXisms that
will cause you trouble.  Assuming you have followed good software coding
practices, porting should be fairly simple.  There are VMS versions of
many UNIX tools.  Most of the GNU tools have been ported to VMS.

I've compiled many UNIX programs on VMS with only a little tweeking of
the CC compile line.  I've also had many UNIX programs that were so
dependent on some UNIX feature, I would have had trouble even porting it
between SYS/V and BSD UNIX variants.

So guess what.  The answer is "It depends on your application."

Oh, DEC used to have some manuals about porting stuff.  I have no idea
if there is anyone left at DEC who could help you.
