> >One of our DECstations died, so we want to use one of the hard drives
> >on a macintosh.  When I connect the hard drive the the mac SCSI


Try jumpering in the "Spin Up Immediately" jumper. DEC sets up their stuff
to not spin up until the host system tells it to (for power sequencing to
avoid tripping breakers). The Mac expects the drive to be spining when it
looks at it. If you have FWB's Hard Disk Toolkit software for the Mac, it
has a menu pick to issue the spin up command if you want to test it before
mucking with jumpers.

