> $       DEFINE DECW$LOGIN_NORESTART TRUE ! process logical...
> $       SET DISPLAY/CREATE/PERM/TRANSPORT='trans'/NODE="''node'"
> $       MCR DECW$STARTLOGIN     ! Fire off the DECwindows Session Manager
> $       WRITE SYS$OUTPUT "DECwindow Session Manager Login initiated on ''f$trnln
> m("SYS$NODE")'"
> $       WRITE SYS$OUTPUT "              for ''node' using transport ''trans'"
> $       WRITE SYS$OUTPUT ""
> $       WAIT 00:00:02           ! Allow user to read the above message
> $       STOP/ID=0               ! Logout silently
> $

I had the same problem.  Turns out that SYS$REM_NODE translates to node-name::
which under V5.5-2 SET DISPLAY/CREATE/NODE=node-name:: likes BUT under V6.1 it
doesn't (probably something to do with phase V node names and the support for
them).  I didn't investigate further.

The fix is to add an: 

	ELSE
		NODE = NODE - "::"

prior to the last ENDIF so that when it's a DECnet node the "::" gets removed.

