>How do I get the workstation to stop sending console output to the Dec
>Windows screen?
>
>Every time someone logs in, or another equally exciting system event occurs,
>it splits the screen and shows you what has happened.  You can get control
>back with Ctrl-F2.  But it's Really annoying.

The only way to COMPLETELY eliminate the ouput is to flip SW3 and hook up s
terminal as the console. But almost all (except for pagefile fragmentation
problems) can be eliminated by:
$ Define/User SYS$COMMAND OPAO:
$ REPLY/DISABLE

I like to have the OPCOM messaged print to my message window by:

$Get_Device:
$ Device = F$GetJPI(F$GetJPI(0,"OWNER"),"TERMINAL")
$ If DEVICE .NES. ""
$ Then
$    Set Process/Priv=Security
$    Define/User SYS$COMMAND 'Device'
$    Reply/Enable/Temp
$    Define/User SYS$COMMAND OPA0:
$    Reply/Disable
$    Set Process/Priv=NoSecurity
$    Exit
$ EndIf
$ Wait 0:0:10
$ GoTo Get_Device

