Robin Jackson (Robin@moneypit.demon.co.uk) wrote:
: In article <398rrv$ecf@hermes.synopsys.com>,
: mattr@Synopsys.com (Matt Richards) wrote:

: >Is it possible to hook up a TK50 to a MAC? If so, how? Please reply

A *real* TK50 is NOT a SCSI device.  A TK50-Z is SCSI compatible.  It is a
question of drive firmware.  It is probably possible to hook a TK50 to a
MAC and write a custom device driver, but I doubt you could get a description
of the command set of the TK50.  The TK50Z should respond as a generic SCSI
tape drive, and any driver that can use the common command set for tapes
should work.  Another problem is that the old TK50's were not very reliable
and were very slow - about 30KB / Sec, when they worked.  We got rid of ours
as soon as we could.


