John,  I'm afraid there is nothing in vanilla flavoured OpenVMS which would 
have done that for you, although there was (maybe still available?) a layered
product called Distributed Time Services Software (DTSS) which can take control
of the system clock away from the raw o/s.

   The current solution from Dec I guess is DECnet/OSI (phase V DECnet) - 
DECnet/OSI includes support for DTSS time servers, with DTSS clients running
on any or all OpenVMS, Ultrix & OSF/1 systems in your network domains.

   I am not aware of any shareware solutions for doing time changes on a single
system without having to purchase a networking product.  

Steve


