In article <3a6b6a$c19@csugrad.cs.vt.edu>, wpugh@csugrad.cs.vt.edu (William T. Pugh) writes:
|> Just curious but what is the name of the graphics board on the 
|> Digital Alpha3000LX AXP computer?
|> 
|> Thanks.

The DEC 3000 Model 300LX AXP comes with integral graphics (HX) on the
system board.

But there are also two TURBOchannel slots, which can hold any of:

 * PXG+ (two slots)
 * ZLX-E1, ZLX-E2, ZLX-E3 (one slot)
 * ZLX-M1 (two slots)
 * ZLX-M2 (three slots, so must be in a TURBOchannel Extender box, or TcE)
 * ZLX-L1 (two slots)

So, the answer is it depends.  But most likely you are asking about the
integral graphics (HX).

