To get access to the machine :
1.  Press reset button on back
2.  When you get the >>> prompt, enter b/1
	This means do a "conversational" boot
3.  When it says "SYSBOOT>" enter "set uafalternate 1"
	This sets the system to use an alternate user authorization file
	If the alternate file doesn't exist, which is normal, then the
	username "SYSTEM" with no password will allow you to log in from
	the console only.
4.  then enter "cont"
	which means continue booting
5.  when VMS is up, login as user "SYSTEM", password <CR>
	I can't possibly imagine running DECWindows on a VS2000.  It 
would take 10-15 minutes to login in DECWindows.  It probably is running
VWS - which is a windowing environment proprietary to DEC.  It runs literally
100 x faster than X-Windows derivatives - too bad its proprietary.


