Umm, the VAX 7000 series contains a VAX 7000 processor.  The VAX 6000 series
contains a VAX 6000 processor.

The 7000 runs a bit faster; has more cache; a different and faster system bus;
a different I/O port arrangement.  The cabinet is different (taller and
deeper); only 1 keyswitch on the front panel; different power supplies (the
power supplies can be backed up with batteries to run the entire cabinet for
some time during a power failure).

