    target_sp = <get_target_sp from jmpbuf>
    if (target_sp < current_sp) {
        generate Invalid Operand Trap
    }
    ....
}

While this check is generally beneficial, it generates an IOT in the case
when longjmp() is called from a signal handler using a temporary stack.
Since the temporary stack is allocated in the data segment and the
stack segment is below both the text and data segments, the test
made in longjmp() will always be true. That is, we have the following
case:

    - target_sp points to an address in the real stack segment
    - current_sp points to an address in the temporary stack in the
      data segment
    - stack segment is in a lower address than the data segment
    - therefore, target_sp is ALWAYS < current_sp --> IOT!


My question: does anyone know of a workaround?  any suggestions on how
	to resolve this problem?

Thanks in advance!


jeremy
