>"Tut! Tut!" cried Sherlock Holmes. "You must act, man, or you are
>lost. Nothing but energy can save you. This is no time for dispair." 


Assuming that you just want to turn a Little-Endian ieee-real into
a Big-Endian ieee-real (or vice versa), it's easy enough to write
such a routine in fortran, something like ...

	INTEGER FUNCTION SWABYT( A, N )
	REAL*4  A(*)
	INTEGER N
C
	REAL*4  RIN, ROUT
	CHAR*1	CIN(4), COUT(4)
	EQUIVALENCE (RIN, CIN)
	EQUIVALENCE (ROUT, COUT)
C
C---    Return 1 on error, 0 on success
C
	IF (N .LT. 1) THEN
		SWABYT = 1
		RETURN
	ENDIF
C
	DO 10 I = 1, N
		RIN = A(I)
		COUT(1) = CIN(4)
		COUT(2) = CIN(3)
		COUT(3) = CIN(2)
		COUT(4) = CIN(1)
		A(I) = ROUT
10	CONTINUE
	SWABYT = 0
	RETURN
	END

(Or should bytes 1-2 and 3-4 be swapped for VAXen?  It shouldn't be
hard to determine by experiment.)

