Looking at the latest issue of inFORM, I noticed that the DEC ATM card
has been announced (somewhere):

>New! TURBOchannel/ATM Adapter
>----------------------------------------------------------------------
>19    DGLTA-FA     ATMworks 750 TURBOchannel-to-ATM adapter      2,995


We have had beta versions of two of these boards & I thought I'd share
our experience. These cards are ATM SONET OC-3 cards.

Between a 3000-600 and 3000-800, we measured ~130 Mbits/s using TCP/IP
(usually a little bit more). By comparison, the best we've ever seen
from a Fore Systems card on boxes other than OSF/1 is 20-40Mb/s,
depending on the card (-100 or -200) and the machine.

Installation and management was simple. We've used the card to do NFS
and FTP across a wide area ATM network. Even the beta boards are very
stable.

When sending from the DEC ATM card to an SGI Indy w/Fore-100 card, we
found that we needed to use the CBR (constant bit rate) feature to
reduce the bit rate to the SGI.  Initially, we were get 25 Mb/s
SGI->DEC, and .2Mb/s DEC->SGI. The problem was that the DEC card was
running so fast it was overflowing the IP buffers on the SGI. We used
the CBR feature to down-grade the DEC card to 25 Mb/s.

