help alleviate my own (and others') desire to see that Seyon
Development be more actively discussed in a public forum.  If you have
ideas on how you would like to see Seyon changed to become more
useful/portable and/or are willing to help with development, please
join this list.

Darin Wayrynen
Seyon Maintainer

(ps.  As mentioned, Seyon is a X11 based terminal emulator, that has
been ported to all major X based workstations, including, but not
limited to: HP-UX, SunOS, Dec, SGI, Linux, BSDi, etc)

