There's a combination clock and battery backed-up memory on a chip on the
system board.  The battery is probably shot.  It's DEC part number 21-32423-01.

The chip is "DALLAS", and has a picture of an alarm clock on the top.  It's in
a socket.  Get a new one, pull the old one, install the new one, re-set your
console's environment variables and you should be all set.

