The
>ODBC drivers we have for RDB only seem to support DECNet and Pathworks
TCP/IP.
>Is there a version which has more generic access ( eg Winsock interface )?

DEC's ODBC driver version 1.1 and above let you use either TCP/IP or IPX. 
This version is distributed with Rdb 6.0 (but you can use it with databases
on earlier versions).  You will also need to install the new SQL/Services
from Rdb 6.0 (seperate installation from Rdb and will work with earlier
versions).  That should be all you need for TCP/IP -- if you want to use IPX
you will need the FSS product from Interconnections on the VMS side.

