Mwm points to the .mwmrc file explicitly with the resource configFile
in the app-defaults file.  On unix, the app-defaults file for mwm is
Mwm in the app-defaults directory or in your home directory.  On VMS
that file is DECW$MWM.DAT and it is in DECW$SYSTEM_DEFAULTS or
DECW$USER_DEFAULTS.  By default, DECW$USER_DEFAULTS points to
SYS$LOGIN (ie: your home directory).  As you are probably aware,
there need not be a user specific app-defaults file.

The easy approach is to copy DECW$MWM.DAT and DECW$MWMRC.DAT (I think
that is the name they use) from DECW$SYSTEM_DEFAULTS to your home
directory.  Edit the app-defaults file and only keep the resources
you want to have different from the default (the rest will fall back
to the system resource file).  For the mwmrc there is NOT a fallback
behavior.  You will have to keep all of the definitions that you
want to use.

In VMS DECwindows, disabling the session manager is a little bit
trickier.  There is a .com file that gets executed.  I think it is
in SYS$SYSTEM (look for decw$*.com).  It would need to be modified
by someone with privs to look for some file in your sys$login
directory and call that instead of the default stuff.  It does not
do this by default.

Dick Schoeller


