In article <aDH0uc2w165w@tcscs.com>, root@tcscs.com
(Gregory Youngblood) writes:

|>I'm looking for any possible upgrade information for the 11/725. I 
|>am under the impression that these are virtually unexpandable and so was 
|>wondering what expansion options there might be.

   Officially, there are no options.  Unofficially, the options
   are extremely limited -- you're probably out of UNIBUS slots,
   and the memory is likely underconfigured.  In other words, no
   options.

   The two controllers commonly supported on the Nebula (VAX-11/730)
   were the IDC and the two-board-set UDA50.  Neither was supported
   on the LCN (VAX-11/725).  And both controllers required an external
   (often 19 inch) rack for mounting the storage devices.

|>Specifically I would like to upgrade hard drive capacity if possible.

   There's no way to expand the configuration in that enclosure.

|>Lastly, I would like to know if there is a UUCP implementation available 
|>for VMS that would run on this system.  If not, what about SLIP software 
|>that would allow setup of FTP daemons and outgoing FTP connections?

   Replace the system with a (used) VAXstation or MicroVAX 3100 series.
   Cheaper, Faster, Smaller, More Efficient, Uses SCSI...  Supported
   under current versions of OpenVMS.  And the parts are easier to get.

   If memory serves, the LCN hasn't been supported since the days of
   VMS V4.7 -- around six or seven years ago.


  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
