  A 725 is really a 730 in a funny looking outfit. The top slot
in the card cage will accept an RB730 controller card, and this
will drive an R80 winchester drive and 2 RL02 10 meg removables.
  
  If you can't find these for free, you aren't looking hard enough...
now, the power, noise and heat will be a lot more than the RC25
was causing, but, if you are using a 725 you are a hardware hacker by nature
and will accept all that for the sheer hell of it.

  If you can't find a drive marked specifcally R80 (came only with
VAX 730), you can use an RM80 in it's place - they were used on
several VAX and PDP 11 models (that's what I used with mine). An
RA80 would probably work as well, with a little fiddling with
the connectors and cables.

  There is a pretty good chance that just about any SMD style
drive could be attached to the RB730 and be made to work, but
my 725 slagged down before I had a chance to try that little
experiment.

