Actually, most of the SPEC bechmarks will work well with that size
cache.

However, the Alphastation 4/233 (Avanti?) uses a 21066 rather than a
21064A. The 21066 has an 8KB on-chip data cache and 8KB on-chip
I-cache. I think it uses the 21064 core, but includes bus logic for
the PCI bus and has a lower pin count (i.e., probably doesn't have as
good an interface to the L2 cache, but I don't know that for a
fact). It was designed for the low-end market.

On the otherhand, the 21064A is a follow-on to the 21064. It has 16KB
I/D-cache, and also has a much faster divide instruction. I think
other things got cleaned up too.

However, the 4/233 would still be 3-5x a Pentium, I think.


