I think that an essential misconception is going on:

In Unix shops the general attitude is "why pay for software if you can
get it for free?" Maintainability, reliability and such cumbersome details
are of no concern, because otherwise they wouldn't be running Unix.

VMS shops are much more prepared to pay money for quality, supported
software. They *KNOW* that maintainability, reliability, etc. are not
free.

