Summary --- 	Request for discussion on tools and techniques of cross
		architecture and operating system version control and develop-
		ment.

Problem:        We are developing UNIX software  for  a  number  of  different
                architectures   (Sun,  Mips,  etc...)  and  operating  systems
                (Ultrix, SunOS 4.1.3, 5.3), simultaneously.   The  purpose  of
                this is two-fold:
                1) This assures that we  are  not  tied  into  one  particular
                hardware/software vendor, and
                2) This assures that our software actually  runs  on  all  the
                platforms it will be asked to run on.

                To achieve this, we are writing using only POSIX system calls,
                use  the GNU compilers, and gnumake.  We have a system of home
                brewed sh, csh, and perl scripts which administrate this.  All
                our files are under source code control (RCS control).

                When our binaries are  made,  they  are  stored  in  different
                locations,   based  on  the  current  ARCH  and  OS,  and  the
                automounter

                While works, it is a bit of overhead for us  to  maintain  our
                system  as  new  OS's come along.  In addition, we have to add
                complexity (i.e. make rules) to it when we  have  to  add  new
                file types.

QUESTIONS:      What systems/products do others use to develop  simultaneously
                on different ARCHES and OS's?

                What methods are used to manage releases of software  so  that
                you  can:  check  on  bugs  in previous revisions, and work on
                updates to new code concurrently?

IMPORTANT:      The  topic  of  developing  for  multiple  architectures   and
                multiple  operating  systems, by its nature, touches many news
                groups.

                This request has  been  cross-posted  to  26  selectived  news
                groups  on  the  North American continent to try to touch on a
                sampling of various cultures but still be responsible  to  net
                band-width.     Please    Follow-up    to   the   one   group,
                "comp.unix.misc", not to the entire list of groups  originally
                posted.  Thanks.
