I'll toss out a hypothesis for you (assuming I understand your
configuration correctly...).

It could be possible that your differential to single-ended converter
is introducing enough delay into the signal propogation time, that
you are occasionally failing to meet some SCSI bus timing parameter
at a device which is sampling the SCSI bus.

You may want to look at the specs for your converter box, and see whether
it imposes any additional restrictions on the systems to which is
connected.  Potential restrictions might include:

	- less than maximum cable lengths (on either or both busses)
	- less than maximum data burst rate 
	- less than maximum number of devices (to reduce electrical bus loading)

If nothing is obvious there, then you will need to put some sort
of monitor device(s) on the SCSI bus(ses), to see what obscure event
is happening.    


