Message-ID: <jbk.783775051@euclid>
NNTP-Posting-Host: euclid.ecs.soton.ac.uk
Summary: X server on DEC alpha OSF1 appears to have a memory leak
Keywords: X server memory leak swap space

Hi,

this is probably very old news, but if it helps anyone avoid the
fustration I've been having...

I couldn't understand why my DEC alpha/OSF1 machine was *always*
running out of swap-space, until I noticed that the X server was
taking 70Mbytes. Because its running under xdm it doesn't get
restarted unless you reboot, at which point it only takes 14Mbytes.

Adding 
DisplayManager._0.terminateServer:      true

to /usr/lib/X11/xdm/xdm-config, and sending a kill -HUP to the xdm
process causes the X server to be shut-down after each session.

This seems to have solved my problem entirely :)

Regards,

James Kingdon.



