> terminated externally.  We have verified that internal terminators have 
> been removed from all drives, except the Sony MO, which we were not able 
> to see without doing more disassembly than we were willing to try.

  You need a terminator on both ends of the bus, and none in the middle. It
sounds like you have 2 terminators near one end of the single-ended bus (the
Sony M/O drive and the "last device"). BTW, what is the total length of the
single-ended bus?

  Some devices just don't cooperate on the SCSI bus - I had one site that had
a Connor drive on a SCSI bus with an Exabyte and some other disks, and the bus
would hang. Removing the Connor fixed things right up.

  You should probably verify that all of your SCSI devices have the latest
version of their firmware. This involves calling all of the manufacturers.

> The problems that we are having some and go sporadically.  We have 
> upgraded cables, swapped CDU interfaces and tried various orderings of 
> drives.

  This system sounds like a real hodgepodge of parts - especially the various
drives stuck in assorted cases. I'd suggest that rather than trying to fix the
current situation, you back up and re-evaluate what you're trying to get out
of this configuration and then try re-implementing it in a more mainstream
manner.

